# Local API examples. Use a REST client or copy each request into your HTTP tool.
# 1. Run the two login requests; obtain user IDs from their user objects or GET /me.
# 2. Copy token/IDs and the latest GET response ETag into the variables below.
# 3. Use a new Idempotency-Key for each NEW command. Retrying the identical command
#    must retain the original key, body and If-Match. Keys below use {{$guid}}.
#    To test a retry, replace {{$guid}} with one fixed UUID for both sends.
# 4. Dates are ISO 8601 instants. Change the example schedule if needed.
# Demo credentials are for the seeded local environment only.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@password = Demo@123456
@employeeToken = PASTE_EMPLOYEE_TOKEN
@managerToken = PASTE_MIDDLE_TOKEN
@profileVersion = PASTE_PROFILE_ROW_VERSION
@employeeId = PASTE_EMPLOYEE_USER_ID
@taskId = PASTE_TASK_ID
@requestId = PASTE_APPROVAL_REQUEST_ID
@logId = PASTE_LOG_ID
@notificationId = PASTE_NOTIFICATION_ID
@jobId = PASTE_JOB_ID
@taskEtag = "1"
@requestEtag = "1"
@logEtag = "1"
@notificationEtag = "1"

### Health performs a database connection check; no authentication required.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Employee login: response {token,tokenType,expiresAt,user}.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"13800000004","password":"{{password}}","accountType":"employee"}

### Manager login: this manager reviews the example employee's self-created tasks.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"13800000002","password":"{{password}}","accountType":"employee"}

### Administrator login uses the original username, even when it is also an employee phone number.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"admin","password":"{{password}}","accountType":"admin"}

# accountType is optional for older clients. Without it, exactly one matching identity/password is
# required; a shared identifier and password returns 409 LOGIN_IDENTITY_AMBIGUOUS. Use the intended
# employee/admin entry point instead of relying on lookup order. Duplicate active employee phone keys
# still return 409 LOGIN_KEY_AMBIGUOUS; only the explicit admin entry bypasses the employee namespace.
# Unknown accountType values return 400 INVALID_INPUT.

### Discover the current server identity. Do not send a client-selected actor ID.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### Four home panels.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/home
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### Effective tasks only. q/from/to/state/priority/assigneeId/creatorId are optional.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks?limit=20&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### Create a task: response provides taskId and requestId.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Local example: supplier review",
  "description": "Compare supplier delivery records.",
  "acceptanceCriteria": "Provide a reviewed comparison and next actions.",
  "assigneeIds": ["{{employeeId}}"],
  "priority": "medium",
  "allDay": false,
  "startAt": "2030-01-14T01:00:00Z",
  "dueAt": "2030-01-17T10:00:00Z"
}

### Applicant queue; pending creations do not appear in the normal task list.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-requests?mine=applicant
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### Manager queue.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-requests?mine=reviewer
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### Read the request snapshot and copy its ETag to requestEtag.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-requests/{{requestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### Approve. For rejection use decision=reject with a nonempty comment.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-requests/{{requestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: {{requestEtag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"decision":"approve"}

### Effective task detail. Copy its latest ETag to taskEtag before any PATCH.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### Definition change requires original-creator permission and a reason.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: {{taskEtag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"command":"change","title":"Local example: supplier review updated","reason":"Clarify scope"}

### Progress requires current-assignee permission and enters review unless exempt.
# Finish/withdraw the preceding pending request, then obtain a fresh task ETag.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: {{taskEtag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"command":"progress","progressNote":"Delivery records collected; comparison in progress."}

### Submit completion; it is not done until the request takes effect.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: {{taskEtag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"command":"complete","completionNote":"Comparison and next actions have been checked."}

### Only the applicant may withdraw a pending request; read its fresh ETag first.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/approval-requests/{{requestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: {{requestEtag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"decision":"withdraw"}

### Reopen a done task, original creator only in this local implementation.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: {{taskEtag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"command":"reopen","reason":"A follow-up correction is required."}

### Own logs; scope=visible expands only to the current user's authorized range.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/work-logs?scope=self&limit=20&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### A log is independent from task approval. taskId is optional and must be visible.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/work-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"body":"Reviewed the supplier data and recorded follow-up questions.","businessDate":"2030-01-14","taskId":"{{taskId}}"}

### Read a log and copy its ETag before editing.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/work-logs/{{logId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### Only the author may edit their log.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/work-logs/{{logId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: {{logEtag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"body":"Reviewed supplier data and confirmed the follow-up owner."}

### Notifications belong to the current user.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications?limit=20&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### Obtain current notification ETag before read/hide.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications/{{notificationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### Reading a notification does not approve it. action=hide hides only this message.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications/{{notificationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: {{notificationEtag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action":"read"}

### Effective, visible task summary.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/analytics/task-summary
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### Local rule-based analysis; no external model is called. `auto` derives the
### statistics/keyword scope and the (possibly narrower) suggestion scope from
### the current role grants. A client may request `self`, but cannot broaden it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai-jobs
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"scopeType":"auto"}

### Owner-only result. The response reports statisticsScope, keywordScope,
### suggestionScope, method=rule_based_local, generatedAt, priority counts and
### pendingComplete. Source tasks and the current authorization version are
### checked again; a stale result returns 409 ANALYSIS_SCOPE_CHANGED.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ai-jobs/{{jobId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### Revoke the current session.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/sessions/current
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sections 1-3 additions: administration, account gate, contacts, and the
# narrower business queries. Add these variables to the block at the top:
#   @adminToken = PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN
#   @newEmployeeId = PASTE_NEW_EMPLOYEE_USER_ID
#   @departmentId = PASTE_DEPARTMENT_ID
#   @positionId = PASTE_POSITION_ID
#   @teamId = PASTE_TEAM_ID
#   @companyItemId = PASTE_COMPANY_ITEM_ID
#   @departmentEtag = "1"
#   @employeeEtag = "1"
#   @companyItemEtag = "1"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Identity only; the one call a forced-password-change session may make besides change/logout.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/session
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}

### First-login and everyday password change. Revokes every session on success.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/password
Authorization: Bearer {{employeeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"currentPassword":"Demo@123456","newPassword":"NewPass12345"}

### Administration overview: departments, positions, teams, roles, constraints.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/organization
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Employee roster. Phone numbers are never echoed; `hasPhone` only reports presence.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Create an employee. The generated initial password is returned exactly once.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"newhire","displayName":"新同事","departmentId":"{{departmentId}}","positionId":"{{positionId}}","level":3,"roleCodes":["employee"]}

### Edit an employee's organization fields. Requires the GET ETag.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/employees/{{newEmployeeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: {{employeeEtag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"teamId":"{{teamId}}"}

### Transfer: moves department/position/team/manager/level/authority and bumps the authorization version.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/employees/{{newEmployeeId}}/transfer
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: {{employeeEtag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"departmentId":"{{departmentId}}","positionId":"{{positionId}}","level":4,"roleCodes":["employee"],"reason":"组织调整"}

### Administrator password reset. The new initial password is returned exactly once.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/employees/{{newEmployeeId}}/password-reset
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

### Departments, positions and teams.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/departments
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"质检部"}

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/departments/{{departmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: {{departmentEtag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"质检一部"}

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/positions
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"质检专员","sortOrder":5}

### Team lead defaults to the creator; an administrator must name an explicit member.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"质检一组","departmentId":"{{departmentId}}","leadUserId":"{{newEmployeeId}}"}

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/teams/{{teamId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: "1"
Content-Type: application/json

{"leadUserId":"{{newEmployeeId}}"}

### Company information (max 10) and the all-day cut-off.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/company
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/company/items
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"公司信息标题","body":"公司信息内容"}

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/company/items/reorder
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderedIds":["{{companyItemId}}"]}

### Stored, validated and audited; the task schedule does not consume it yet (section 6).
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/company/off-work-time
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"offWorkTime":"17:30"}

### Dispatch candidates: the dispatch range only, narrower than what the caller may view.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignee-candidates?q=张
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### Log author filter (list + tree) limited to self and direct reports.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/work-log-authors
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### Personal profile, including the saved avatar and current rowVersion.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}

### Replace profileVersion with the rowVersion from the preceding read.
### avatar: rabbit/cat/bear/panda, null to clear, or a validated PNG/JPEG data URI.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
If-Match: "{{profileVersion}}"
Content-Type: application/json

{"avatar":"rabbit"}
